**Project Overview:**
The News Intelligence Platform is an enterprise-grade full-stack application designed to combat information overload. It automatically aggregates global news via an automated cron-based ingestion pipeline, processes the content using OpenAI, and visualizes macro trends on a highly responsive analytics dashboard. 

**Key Technologies:**
*   **Frontend:** Next.js 15, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, TanStack React Query, Zustand
*   **Backend:** Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB Atlas (Mongoose), Redis
*   **AI Integration:** OpenAI API (`gpt-4o-mini`)
*   **Infrastructure:** Vercel, Render

**Core Features Implemented:**
*   **AI Processing Pipeline:** Engineered a highly optimized OpenAI integration that extracts 2-sentence summaries, sentiment classification, and key insights in a single, token-efficient JSON response.
*   **Advanced Search & URL Synchronization:** Migrated frontend filtering state to URL Query Parameters, enabling deep-linking, bookmarkable queries, and a seamless native browser experience.
*   **Analytics Dashboard:** Implemented a real-time visualization layer using Recharts to display sentiment distributions and trending categories.
*   **Production-Grade Security & Performance:** Integrated tiered Redis-backed rate limiting, pinned JWT authentication, NoSQL/XSS injection guards, and Mongoose `.lean()` queries for ultra-fast data retrieval.

I have included a comprehensive `README.md` within the repository that details the architecture, API endpoints, and instructions for running the project locally. 

Thank you again for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to walk the engineering team through my code, discuss my architectural decisions, and explore how my skills align with the goals of your team.

